================================================================================
STEP-BY-STEP INSTRUCTIONS FROM STEP ZERO (WHERE TO CLICK)
================================================================================

--- STEP 1: CREATE PROJECT IN VISUAL STUDIO ---
1. Open Visual Studio.
2. Click "Create a new project".
3. In the top search box, type: ASP.NET Core Web API
4. Select the template named:
   "ASP.NET Core Web API" (verify it displays the C# tag).
5. Click "Next".
6. Configure project details:
   - Project name: StudentAPI
   - Location: Choose your preferred directory.
7. Click "Next".
8. In the "Additional information" screen:
   - Framework: Select .NET 6.0, .NET 7.0, or .NET 8.0.
   - Authentication type: None.
   - Ensure "Use controllers (uncheck to use minimal APIs)" is CHECKED.
   - Check "Configure for HTTPS".
9. Click "Create".

--- STEP 2: CREATE MODELS FOLDER AND STUDENT MODEL CLASS ---
1. In Solution Explorer on the right, right-click the project name "StudentAPI".
2. Hover over "Add" -> click "New Folder".
3. Name the folder: Models
4. Right-click the newly created "Models" folder.
5. Hover over "Add" -> click "Class...".
6. Set the Name at the bottom to:
   Student.cs
7. Click "Add".
8. Delete all default code in "Student.cs", paste the complete code from FILE 1 below, and save (Ctrl + S).

--- STEP 3: CREATE THE API CONTROLLER ---
1. In Solution Explorer, right-click the "Controllers" folder.
   (If it does not exist, right-click the project -> Add -> New Folder -> name it "Controllers").
2. Hover over "Add" -> click "Controller...".
3. In the left categories panel, click "API".
4. In the center list, select:
   "API Controller - Empty"
5. Click "Add".
6. In the prompt dialog, set the Controller name to:
   StudentController.cs
7. Click "Add".
8. Delete all default code in "StudentController.cs", paste the complete code from FILE 2 below, and save (Ctrl + S).

--- STEP 4: VERIFY PROGRAM.CS ---
1. Open "Program.cs" in Solution Explorer.
2. Verify that controller mapping services are enabled (see FILE 3).
3. Save (Ctrl + S).

--- STEP 5: RUN AND TEST THE WEB API ---
1. Press F5 (or Ctrl + F5) or click the green Play button ("https" / "IIS Express") at the top toolbar.
2. The default browser window will launch.
3. In the address bar, append `/api/Student` to the URL:
   Example: https://localhost:7032/api/Student
4. The browser will display the student records formatted as JSON.

