================================================================================
KEY CONCEPTS EXPLANATION (VIVA REFERENCE):
================================================================================
1. [ApiController]          : Enables API-specific features including attribute routing requirements and automatic HTTP 400 bad request responses.
2. [Route("api/[controller]")]: Token-based routing attribute where [controller] takes the prefix name of the class ("Student"), creating the route /api/Student.
3. ControllerBase           : Base class for Web API controllers that omits view-rendering support found in standard MVC Controller classes.
4. [HttpGet]                : Action method selector restricting execution exclusively to incoming HTTP GET requests.
5. Automatic JSON Parsing   : ASP.NET Core uses System.Text.Json by default to serialize C# object collections into clean JSON text.
